.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_bsr \- set \(rsR convention
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBint\fP pcre2_set_bsr(\fBpcre2_compile_context\fP *\fIccontext\fP, \fBuint32_t\fP \fIvalue\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function sets the convention for processing \f(CR\(rsR\fP within a compile context.
The second argument must be one of \fBPCRE2_BSR_ANYCRLF\fP or \fBPCRE2_BSR_UNICODE\fP. The
result is zero for success or \fBPCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA\fP if the second argument is
invalid.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.